course: dictionary
lesson: 7837
title: Words about racehorses
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A racehorse is a horse that is bred and trained to run in races. Bred means people chose its parents and raised it for speed, and trained means it practises running. Context helps here: «A galloping racehorse can reach about 70 kilometres an hour over a short distance.» Galloping and reach tell you it is running very fast.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Could you say "a galloping horse can reach about 70 kilometres an hour"? The sentence still makes sense, but racehorse adds the clue that it is a horse for racing.
explain: Racehorses are usually fast, slim breeds such as Thoroughbreds. A breed is a type of animal with shared features, so a Thoroughbred is one kind of racehorse. Phrases like «a champion racehorse» and «racehorse trainer» show you what a racehorse is and who works with it.
explain: Racehorse is made of two smaller words, race and horse. Race is a contest to see who is first, and horse is the animal. Spotting small words inside a big word is a useful reading trick.
fact: A racehorse is a horse bred and trained to run in races.
fact: Racehorses are usually fast, slim breeds such as Thoroughbreds.
fact: «A champion racehorse» is a racehorse that wins a lot of races and is among the best.
fact: A racehorse trainer is the person who prepares the horse for races.
fact: Famous races with racehorses include the Grand National in the UK, the Melbourne Cup in Australia and the Kentucky Derby in the US.
exercise: «A galloping racehorse can reach about 70 kilometres an hour over a short distance.» What is a racehorse? | A horse that only sleeps | A pony that lives in a field | *A horse that is bred and trained to run in races | A horse that pulls a cart on a farm
exercise: Which breed is an example of a racehorse? | Clydesdale | Shetland pony | *Thoroughbred | Donkey
exercise: Who prepares a racehorse for races? | *A racehorse trainer | A tour guide at the stables | A farmer who grows hay | A vet who only checks teeth
test: Which famous race is held in Australia? | Grand National | Kentucky Derby | Tour de France | *Melbourne Cup
test: In «a champion racehorse», what does champion mean? | Sleepy and slow | *One of the best, a winner of many races | Very small | Newly born
exam: Which two smaller words make up racehorse? | horse and house | rate and hoarse | race and hose | *race and horse
